error[ffi_parameter_type]: `p` of `fill` is declared `u8`, and the header's `char *` points at a different width or sign — clang read the header, and C writes back exactly the bytes the header expects
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-163-a-plain-char-pointee-bound-as-u8-is-refused.hero:10:20
     |
  10 |     function fill(@p: u8)  #~ ffi_parameter_type
     |                    ^
  note: §4.19: a C out-parameter is an `@` parameter, and what it points at is held to the header's own width and sign — `u64` where it says `size_t *`, `i32` where it says `int *`
  fix (guess): declare `p` as `@p: i8`
